      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Lubricating oil, sometimes simply called lubricant/lube, is a class of oils used to reduce the friction, heat, and wear between mechanical components that are in contact with each other. It is used in motorized vehicles, where it is known specifically as motor oil and transmission fluid. Petroleum-derived lubricating oil is a mixture produced by atmospheric and vacuum distillation of selected paraffinic and naphthenic crude oils, after which chemical changes may be required to produce the desired properties of the refined product.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "润滑油，有时简称为润滑剂/润滑油，是一类用于减少相互接触的机械部件之间的摩擦、热量和磨损的油类。它主要用于机动车辆，具体称为机油和传动液。石油衍生润滑油是一种通过大气蒸馏和真空蒸馏精选石蜡原油和环烷原油而制成的混合物，之后可能需要进行化学变化，以获得所需的精炼产品特性。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
